      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'll try the eBPF stuff, might be a bit of a pain to set up but worth a shot. but honestly, even with all that, it just feels so senseless. like, everything is \"correct\" on paper, the infra is stable, the code is tested locally, and yet it just breaks in this weird, unpredictable way in the middle of the night sometimes. it's like something is actively sabotaging it. is there any way to log the exact state of the virtual network interface the moment the reset happens so i can see if it's a legitimate drop or something more malicious?",
